  "description": "⭐ <em>Light up the night and enjoy a magical evening filled with love and connection at the </em><strong><em>Water Lantern Festival</em></strong><em>! After captivating thousands in New York, Los Angeles, and Toronto, this unforgettable experience arrives in London. Gather your loved ones for a beautiful evening of reflection, joy, and glowing lanterns floating on the water. Watch as thousands of illuminated lanterns create a breathtaking display, symbolising hope, healing, and togetherness.</em><br>\r\n<br>\r\n<strong>🏮✨ Be part of the magic. Tickets are now available. Secure your spot before they're gone.🚨</strong><br>\r\n<br>\r\n<strong>Highlights</strong><br>\r\n💖 Personalise and release your lantern onto the water at sunset, creating a glowing spectacle of light and love<br>\r\n🎶 Relaxing melodies and unique performances set the perfect atmosphere<br>\r\n🍔 Delicious food and unique offerings from local artisans<br>\r\n🔍 Fun activities to enjoy and connect with other attendees, such as a treasure hunt<br>\r\n✨ Share stories, laughter, and memories with old friends and new connections<br>\r\n<br>\r\n💫 <strong>Want to make your night even more special?</strong> The <strong>Couples Pack</strong> also includes a picnic blanket, so all you have to do is find the perfect spot, sit back, and enjoy the event. 🧺🌅 😉 <strong>And yes...</strong> even if you're coming with friends or family, this pack is for you too!<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<strong>General Info</strong><br>\r\n📍 <strong>South East London: Danson Park</strong>\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>📅 <strong>Date:</strong> Saturday, 5th September 2026</li>\r\n\t<li>📌 Danson Park Boating Pool, 51 Danson Rd, Bexleyheath DA6 8HL, <u>51.452508, 0.117002</u></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<br>\r\n📍 <strong>South West London:&nbsp;Clapham Common</strong>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>📅 <strong>Dates:</strong>&nbsp;Saturday 19th and Sunday 20th September 2026</li>\r\n\t<li>📌 Clapham Common, Long Pond, <u>51.459531, -0.142831</u></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n🕒 Time: the festival starts at 6 PM and the lanterns will be released between 7 PM and 8 PM<br>\r\n⏳ Duration: approx. 4 hours<br>\r\n👤 Age requirement: all ages are welcome! Perfect for families, couples, and groups of friends<br>\r\n♿ Accessibility: the venues are wheelchair accessible<br>\r\n❓ Please consult the FAQs of this experience <a href=\"https://eu.waterlanternfestival.com/london/#faqs\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">here</a><br>\r\n🎁 Gift memories to someone special! Purchase a gift card <a href=\"https://feverup.com/m/704919\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">here</a><br>\r\n<br>\r\n<strong>Description</strong><br>\r\nGet ready for a night you’ll never forget! Whether you want to honour the past, celebrate the present, or dream about the future, the <em>Water Lantern Festival </em>offers a magical setting to create lifelong memories. Bring your friends, your family, or come on your own; one thing is certain: you’ll leave with a full heart and a brighter spirit. Get your tickets now for the <em>Water Lantern Festival </em>in London!<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<strong>Commitment to the Planet</strong><br>\r\nAt the <em>Water Lantern Festival</em>, our goal is to leave every place better than we found it. Following a \"leave no trace\" philosophy, we collect every lantern after the event and even remove any pre-existing waste from the water. Our lanterns are 100% sustainable: made from biodegradable rice paper, wooden bases, and LED candles that are reused and recycled to reduce our environmental footprint.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nHelp us protect the environment! To make this a truly green event, we need your support:\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>Use the recycling stations for your personal waste.</li>\r\n\t<li>Make sure not to leave any rubbish in green areas or near the water.</li>\r\n</ul>",
